  "prompt_original": "fix(parser): parse ALTER TABLE DROP with multiple columns (#8486)\n\n* fix(parser): parse ALTER TABLE DROP with multiple columns\n\nALTER TABLE t DROP COLUMN a, b fell back to parsing as a Command\nbecause only the first column was consumed and the comma-separated\ncontinuation had no DROP keyword for the CSV action parser to match.\n\nParse the continuation columns as additional Drop actions with the\nsame kind. (GH#8485)\n\n* fix(parser): keep multi-column DROP COLUMN in one action per dialect flag\n\nPer the review on GH#8486, splitting `ALTER TABLE t DROP COLUMN a, b`\ninto separate Drop actions broke three things: Snowflake and T-SQL\nreject the generated `DROP COLUMN a, DROP COLUMN b` with a syntax\nerror, calling `_parse_drop_column` directly skipped MySQL's\n`_parse_alter_drop_action` (so `DROP PRIMARY KEY` became a Command),\nand MySQL options after a DROP got parsed as columns (`DROP COLUMN a,\nALGORITHM=INPLACE` raised a ParseError).\n\nFollow the `ALTER_TABLE_ADD_REQUIRED_FOR_EACH_COLUMN` pattern: add an\n`ALTER_TABLE_DROP_REQUIRED_FOR_EACH_COLUMN` flag (False for Snowflake\nand T-SQL). In the base `_parse_alter_drop_action`, when the flag is\noff and the action is a `DROP COLUMN` followed by a comma, parse the\nrest into the same `exp.Drop`'s `tables`, like `DROP TABLE a, b`.\n`_parse_alter_table_drop` stays as is, and `drop_sql` round-trips the\nresult as-is.\n\nTests: the multi-column identities moved to test_snowflake.py /\ntest_tsql.py, `DROP COLUMN a, ALGORITHM=INPLACE` and a DropPrimaryKey\naction assertion were added to test_mysql.py, and the generic parser\ntest now asserts a single exp.Drop with multiple tables.\n\n* style: fix ruff-format violation in multi-column DROP test\n\nWrap the chained assert_is call in test_mysql.py the way ruff format\nexpects; the previous wrapping was rejected by the ruff-format hook in\n'make style' (Makefile:120, pre-commit run --all-files). Formatting\nonly - no behavioral change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Weijian He <230282609+Madin-H23@users.noreply.github.com>",
